Comment: "// @@@ If fromIndex is non-negative and a set bit is found, then all bits from fromIndex up to but not including the found set bit index are false."

We are inside method nextSetBit(int fromIndex). The method returns index of next set bit >= fromIndex, or -1 if none.

Spec: If fromIndex >=0 and a set bit is found (i.e., result != -1), then for all i such that fromIndex <= i < result, get(i) == false.

We need to use observers: this.get(int). That's public method get(bitIndex). So we can refer to this.get(i). Use \result for return value.

Premise: fromIndex >=0 && \result != -1 => for all int i; fromIndex <= i && i < \result; !this.get(i). (or this.get(i) == false).

Thus assert: assert (fromIndex >= 0 && \result != -1) => \forall int i; fromIndex <= i && i < \result; !this.get(i); 

Make sure syntax: !this.get(i) is boolean. Could also write this.get(i) == false.

Thus final code:

<code>assert (fromIndex >= 0 && \result != -1) => \forall int i; fromIndex <= i && i < \result; this.get(i) == false;</code>

